formal.sva:
// Assert that when range_regwen is not locked and a memory range write enable is active, the driven net does not falsely enable DMA access.
// Since the exact intended safe state of driven_net is unknown, this property only monitors the condition and flags the event for review.
// Status: UNCERTAIN, formalizability partial.
wire condition = prim_mubi_pkg::mubi4_test_false_loose(prim_mubi_pkg::mubi4_t'(reg2hw.range_regwen.q)) && (reg2hw.enabled_memory_range_base.qe || reg2hw.enabled_memory_range_limit.qe);
assert property (@(posedge clk_i) disable iff (!rst_ni) condition |-> ##0 (driven_net != 1) else $error("Potential unintended DMA window enable: range_regwen unlocked while memory range write enable active"));
